      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7e278ba1-0753-5ad1-acd1-7444ecae3dd7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles Dill, Jean-Philippe Rameau, Voltaire, Giacomo Puccini, Henri Larrivée\n- Works: Castor et Pollux, Samson, Manon Lescaut\n- Topics: opera composition, revivals, performance debuts\n\nFacts:\n- Charles Dill proposes that Jean-Philippe Rameau composed Castor et Pollux in 1737 just after working with Voltaire on the unfinished opera Samson.\n- Charles Dill states that Jean-Philippe Rameau implemented Voltaire's aesthetics in Castor et Pollux.\n- Henri Larrivée made his first solo appearance as a high priest in a 1755 revival of Jean-Philippe Rameau's Castor et Pollux.\n- Giacomo Puccini composed the four-act opera Manon Lescaut between 1890 and 1893.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
